# Admin bilingual configuration layout

When adding or editing bilingual fields in the admin dashboard (`AdminDashboardClient.tsx` and related admin components), follow the existing site convention:

- Use a two-column grid (`grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-3` or `gap-6`).
- **Left column:** French field (`*_ht`, `*_kreyol`, `nameFr`, `addressFr`, labels ending in `(Français)`).
- **Right column:** English field (`*_en`, `*_english`, `nameEn`, `addressEn`, labels ending in `(English)`).
- Keep paired rows aligned: French name above French address, English name above English address.

Do not place English on the left and French on the right.

The French side of bilingual labels must be **standard French**, not Haitian Creole (no `Imaj`, `Jou`, `Kwayans`, `Misyon`, etc.).

Match label style used elsewhere (uppercase, small, slate-400/500).
